li-vi-p2 = prose (cons "An assessor concludes P only when it holds a construction of P over every history compatible with what it observed (hyperactivity v31, §1, equation 1.3). To call a belief delusional is to assert its falsehood: a construction of not-P over the assessor's whole fiber. Where the belief concerns what the assessor cannot observe (another's mathematics, record, or inner state), histories in which it is true remain, and the only valid conclusion is “not established for me”. A label assigned from base rates (“bipolar”, “talks of his own exceptional ability”) is a conclusion over the fiber of the average patient, not of this person, and asserts a falsehood it has not shown. Self-assessment that matches the record is accurate. Every human being is unlike every other; that is not a symptom." nil)
